<%- include("./header") %>

<main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-10 max-w-3xl">
    <header>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900">What ToyHub keeps, and why</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">
            This page explains the information the shop needs to work. It describes what the
            application actually stores, in plain words.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500">
            Last updated: <%= new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { month: "long", year: "numeric" }) %>
        </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
        <section class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Your account</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">
                We keep the name, email address and phone number you sign up with, plus any
                delivery addresses you save. A password is stored only as a one-way hash.
                Signing in with Google stores the Google account id linked to the same email.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Your orders and activity</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">
                Orders, their items and status, invoices, wallet balance and top-ups, reviews,
                wishlist entries and applied coupons belong to your account. They are used to
                fulfil orders, show your history, and keep offers and reviews fair.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Your session</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">
                A session cookie keeps you signed in. A second token protects forms from being
                submitted by another site. Both are cleared when you log out.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Services that help</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">
                The shop uses a database host, an image host for product pictures, a payment
                provider for card and wallet payments, and an email provider for verification
                and password-reset codes. Each receives only what its task needs.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Your choices</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">
                You can change your name, phone number and addresses from your account at any
                time. To ask for a copy of your account data, or for the account to be removed,
                contact us and we will work through it with you.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 bg-green-50 border border-green-100 rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Questions about privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Write to <a href="mailto:toyhub@gmail.com" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:text-green-700">toyhub@gmail.com</a> and say what you would like to know.</p>
    </div>
</main>

<%- include("./footer") %>
